---
description: One responsibility per component, hook, and class
globs: apps/web/**/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: false
---
# Responsibility

A component, hook, or class has one reason to change. A short helper used only there may stay in the same file as a private function.

A component renders one region and may hold that region's UI state, such as a search string or an open row. Filtering, aggregation, and formatting that take more than a few lines move to a named function or to the hook that owns the data.

When the returned JSX has several regions a reader would name, each region is its own component in the same folder. One component per file still applies.

A hook answers one question. A hook that only composes other hooks stays thin. Mapping goes to a mapper. The hook calls that mapper. UI state stays in the component.

A hook used by one feature lives next to that feature. A hook shared by several features lives in `src/hooks`.

A class does one job. A method that does not use `this` is a function. Do not split a class or a service file that is already one task, such as an API client, `DraftOdds`, or the performance stats.

Do not extract a single element, a status line, a hook that only forwards one query, or a helper of a few lines used once.

```tsx
// Bad: the screen filters the catalog and renders every region
const classes = picks.classes.flatMap((heroClass) => heroClass.heroes.filter((hero) => hero.name.includes(needle)));
return (
  <Panel>
    <DraftTeam slots={picks.allySlots} />
    {classes.map((heroClass) => (
      <ThumbGrid key={heroClass.id} />
    ))}
  </Panel>
);

// Good: the grid owns the search
<DraftHeroes classes={picks.classes} taken={picks.taken} onToggle={picks.toggleHero} />
```
